 "title": "Four integration styles",
 "description": "File transfer: ERP writes a nightly asset file that analytics reads later. Shared database: the CRM and the portal both read and write the portal database. Remote procedure invocation: the portal calls the ERP read API and waits for the reply. Messaging: the CRM publishes an event to a channel, and the work-order integration consumes it later. Dashed arrows show asynchronous transfer; solid arrows show synchronous access.",
